{"total_count":39,"incomplete_results":false,"items":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/4419","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/4419/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/4419/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/4419/events","html_url":"https://github.com/valhalla/valhalla/issues/4419","id":2015523637,"node_id":"I_kwDOAvqbUc54InM1","number":4419,"title":"Pedestrians appear unable to leave sidewalks, rendering pedestrian routing in cities poorly supported","user":{"login":"jorisgeer","id":7885507,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4ODU1MDc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7885507?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jorisgeer","html_url":"https://github.com/jorisgeer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jorisgeer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jorisgeer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jorisgeer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jorisgeer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jorisgeer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jorisgeer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jorisgeer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jorisgeer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jorisgeer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":313657473,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMTM2NTc0NzM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/labels/wontfix","name":"wontfix","color":"ffffff","default":true,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":23,"created_at":"2023-11-28T23:51:54Z","updated_at":"2025-01-16T11:12:12Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"In OpenStreetMap data, sidewalks are typically drawn separate from the road, even if there is no kerb in between. Thus, when routing, there is no physical connection to the road and walkers are routed all the way around any physical connection.\r\nThe concept of 'crossing a road', leaving a sidewalk, does not exist. That makes pedestrian routing in a city with many sidewalks poorly supported and comes with odd detours.\r\nGoogle Maps appears not to draw sidewalks as such, avoiding the issue. But once they are properly drawn, then routing software should understand how walkers walk on them and how road crossings work.\r\n\r\nSee screenshot for a typical example. The footpath is adjacent to the local road, as usual. If there are no sideways at the same side of the road, the detour can be infinite. Just as long as it takes to have that physical (in OSM terms) connection.\r\n\r\n![Screenshot 2023-11-29 at 9 48 11 am](https://github.com/valhalla/valhalla/assets/7885507/5cf211da-bc22-46ff-bf57-4aeedf0ba080)\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/4419/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/4419/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/42","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/42/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/42/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/42/events","html_url":"https://github.com/valhalla/valhalla/issues/42","id":204678094,"node_id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyMDQ2NzgwOTQ=","number":42,"title":"Area Ways","user":{"login":"kevinkreiser","id":697548,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5NzU0OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/697548?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinkreiser","html_url":"https://github.com/kevinkreiser","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinkreiser/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinkreiser/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinkreiser/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinkreiser/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinkreiser/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinkreiser/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinkreiser/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinkreiser/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinkreiser/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":530254183,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw1MzAyNTQxODM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/labels/mjolnir","name":"mjolnir","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[{"login":"gknisely","id":2676277,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676277?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gknisely","html_url":"https://github.com/gknisely","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gknisely/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gknisely/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gknisely/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gknisely/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gknisely/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gknisely/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gknisely/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gknisely/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gknisely/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2017-02-01T19:18:56Z","updated_at":"2026-09-11T15:54:46Z","closed_at":"2026-09-11T15:54:46Z","assignee":{"login":"gknisely","id":2676277,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676277?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gknisely","html_url":"https://github.com/gknisely","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gknisely/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gknisely/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gknisely/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gknisely/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gknisely/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gknisely/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gknisely/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gknisely/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gknisely/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"(2016-02-16T14:20:07Z) @kevinkreiser : originally created valhalla/mjolnir#389\r\n\r\nSome ways are marked as `area=yes` in a lot of cases this ends up being a polygon and not something that is routable. So currently we throw away all ways marked like this.\n\nThe problem is, this does throw out some valid routable information. Go here http://taginfo.openstreetmap.org/tags/area=yes#combinations and refine it with `highway` to see of all marked `area=yes` what values of `highway` occur.\n\n![bildschirmfoto vom 2016-02-16 09 14 24](https://cloud.githubusercontent.com/assets/697548/13078540/bc72d048-d48d-11e5-9c23-e593f7d73927.png)\n\nYou'll notice that there are a lot of pedestrian stuff. Now it may be little pedestrian islands not connected to anything else but if its large enough we might want to still keep it (university on campus pedestrian routing routing?)\n\nSo there are a couple of things we could do. Perhaps we should, as @gknisely suggested, not throw away any area features. After all, if the other attribution on the way (the `highway` tag) makes the way seem not routable it should weed out stuff that is just polygons. Another check we could do is make sure the geometry is not a ring. This is good for most cases but you could see cases (none in taginfo though..) where its a `junction=roundabout` that might be marked as area as well as being routable.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/42/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/42/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/3736","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/3736/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/3736/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/3736/events","html_url":"https://github.com/valhalla/valhalla/issues/3736","id":1367785669,"node_id":"I_kwDOAvqbUc5RhsDF","number":3736,"title":"No routing around highway=pedestrian areas","user":{"login":"FranckRobin","id":112408722,"node_id":"U_kgDOBrM4kg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/112408722?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FranckRobin","html_url":"https://github.com/FranckRobin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FranckRobin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FranckRobin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FranckRobin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FranckRobin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FranckRobin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FranckRobin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FranckRobin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FranckRobin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FranckRobin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":313657469,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMTM2NTc0Njk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","color":"84b6eb","default":true,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2022-09-09T12:51:07Z","updated_at":"2023-05-16T23:15:04Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"I understand from previous issues that there is no plan for pedestrian to route via highway=platform (#3691), or through areas (#17), but it would be very useful to route at least around highway=pedestrian areas (following their outer).\r\nI did it successfully with OSRM and GraphHopper (in https://www.openstreetmap.org), but not with valhalla and mapbox whatever the settings (including default ones).\r\nThis leads to very incorrect paths in cases similar as the one below with a 16km path versus the real path of 16m...\r\nhttps://valhalla.openstreetmap.de/directions?profile=pedestrian&wps=5.374277830123902%2C43.29464496683285%2C5.374014973640443%2C43.29465668009512\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/112408722/189351861-55ea2703-af8b-4761-baa1-1385e83a669a.png)\r\nThe involved highway=pedestrian example is https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/232715149\r\nThe expected outer path is the same as with OSRM and GraphHopper:\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/112408722/189357479-60cdd67a-661c-4a0c-a10b-6029994d406f.png)\r\nCould you please suggest a workaround or better offer a solution? Thank you by advance\r\n\r\n\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/3736/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/3736/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/4978","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/4978/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/4978/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/4978/events","html_url":"https://github.com/valhalla/valhalla/issues/4978","id":2667755807,"node_id":"I_kwDOAvqbUc6fArkf","number":4978,"title":"pedestrian one-way should only be respected for `oneway:foot` tags","user":{"login":"hkavsm","id":184198774,"node_id":"U_kgDOCvqmdg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184198774?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hkavsm","html_url":"https://github.com/hkavsm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hkavsm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hkavsm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hkavsm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hkavsm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hkavsm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hkavsm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hkavsm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hkavsm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hkavsm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":8973734553,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAvqbUc8AAAACFuBSmQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/labels/pedestrian","name":"pedestrian","color":"1675e8","default":false,"description":"problems with pedestrian costing model","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2024-11-18T09:08:10Z","updated_at":"2026-09-09T12:56:15Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"I'm new to GitHub, so I hope I'm doing this right.\r\n\r\nI have noticed that (shared) paths for cyclists and pedestrians that are one-way for cyclists are being treated as also one-way for pedestrians (the routing for pedestrians is the same).\r\n\r\nExample: https://www.openstreetmap.org/directions?engine=fossgis_valhalla_foot&route=49.010416%2C8.381480%3B49.010438%2C8.381893#map=19/49.010506/8.382700&layers=N","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/4978/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/4978/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/5753","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/5753/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/5753/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/5753/events","html_url":"https://github.com/valhalla/valhalla/issues/5753","id":3687231181,"node_id":"I_kwDOAvqbUc7bxq7N","number":5753,"title":"Bicycle routing should default to dismount access on footways/pedestrian highways, currently excluded","user":{"login":"ftrebien","id":3969479,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5Njk0Nzk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3969479?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ftrebien","html_url":"https://github.com/ftrebien","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ftrebien/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ftrebien/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ftrebien/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ftrebien/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ftrebien/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ftrebien/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ftrebien/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ftrebien/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ftrebien/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":11,"created_at":"2025-12-02T19:17:20Z","updated_at":"2026-08-03T13:55:10Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Valhalla currently avoids routing bicycles over `highway=footway` and `highway=pedestrian` unless these ways have tags such as `bicycle=dismount`, `bicycle=yes`, `bicycle=permissive`, etc. The router should assume that pushing a bike is generally legal in most footpaths at walking speed, so these ways would still be somewhat strongly avoided unless when they're useful shortcuts. Only `bicycle=no` should be treated as strict prohibition even for pushing.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/5753/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/5753/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/4657","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/4657/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/4657/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/4657/events","html_url":"https://github.com/valhalla/valhalla/issues/4657","id":2206163260,"node_id":"I_kwDOAvqbUc6Df2E8","number":4657,"title":"pedestrian avoids sidewalk and takes primary","user":{"login":"tatobox","id":153958793,"node_id":"U_kgDOCS05iQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/153958793?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tatobox","html_url":"https://github.com/tatobox","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tatobox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tatobox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tatobox/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tatobox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tatobox/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tatobox/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tatobox/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tatobox/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tatobox/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":894634455,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw4OTQ2MzQ0NTU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/labels/investigate","name":"investigate","color":"d8352f","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":8973734553,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAvqbUc8AAAACFuBSmQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/labels/pedestrian","name":"pedestrian","color":"1675e8","default":false,"description":"problems with pedestrian costing model","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":8,"created_at":"2024-03-25T16:28:07Z","updated_at":"2025-07-20T14:07:43Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Hi everyone,\r\nWhen I create a walking route the track goes on the road and does not follow the sidewalk.\r\nIn URL just a short example but it happens often. Is this a problem that needs to be corrected in iD Editor or a routing problem in Valhalla?\r\nWith OSMAnd on iOS the routing is correct\r\n[https://valhalla.openstreetmap.de/directions?profile=pedestrian&wps=11.325772404670715%2C44.4969071020134%2C11.327086687088014%2C44.497898125113466](url)\r\nIt should look like the blue line in the screenshot.\r\n<table style=\"width:100%\">\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td><img src=\"https://github.com/gis-ops/valhalla-app/assets/153958793/c6160e35-a3cb-4da6-8792-dfed2d082486)\"  width=\"300\" height=\"auto\"/> </td>\r\n    <td><img src=\"https://github.com/gis-ops/valhalla-app/assets/153958793/def055da-391c-4f0d-b0db-4c4371036d8c)\"  width=\"300\" height=\"auto\"/> </td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n</table>","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/4657/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/4657/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/3469","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/3469/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/3469/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/3469/events","html_url":"https://github.com/valhalla/valhalla/issues/3469","id":1087227630,"node_id":"I_kwDOAvqbUc5Azcbu","number":3469,"title":"Indoor routing support proposal","user":{"login":"liyinxiao","id":37345111,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MzQ1MTEx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37345111?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/liyinxiao","html_url":"https://github.com/liyinxiao","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liyinxiao/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liyinxiao/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liyinxiao/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liyinxiao/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liyinxiao/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liyinxiao/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liyinxiao/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liyinxiao/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liyinxiao/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":313657469,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMTM2NTc0Njk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","color":"84b6eb","default":true,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":9,"created_at":"2021-12-22T22:20:05Z","updated_at":"2025-06-05T16:19:46Z","closed_at":"2025-06-05T16:19:45Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Pedestrians should be able to navigate through indoor elements such as corridors, elevators, stairs, escalators, and/or building entrances. OSM already supports indoor mapping, although adoption has not been very high. I am writing this proposal to see if there's any interest in supporting pedestrian indoor routing in valhalla. Briefly, here are a few potential use cases: \r\n- Corridors\r\n    - Pedestrians can walk through corridors\r\n- Elevator/stairs/escalators\r\n    - Pedestrians can take elevator/stairs/escalators to a different level\r\n- Building Entrance\r\n    - Pedestrian can enter/exit buildings through building entrances\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/37345111/147153056-dab79fa5-ebef-455a-9774-29e4f3564116.png)\r\n*An example of indoor routing: this route goes through a mall (Prudential center, Boston), a footbridge, and a second mall (Copley Place, Boston).*\r\n\r\n\r\n### Proposed data model of indoor elements\r\nOSM has a few tagging schemas for indoor mapping, including [Simple Indoor Tagging (SIT)](https://wiki.openstreetmap.org/wiki/Simple_Indoor_Tagging) as well as [indoor tagging schemes](https://wiki.openstreetmap.org/wiki/Indoor_Mapping#Tagging_proposals). To build routing graphs, SIT polygons are probably not the best fit, and I am proposing this list of indoor elements as a starting point for valhalla routing service to support:\r\n\r\n- [Corridors](https://wiki.openstreetmap.org/wiki/Tag:highway%3Dcorridor)\r\n    - Way: tag:highway=corridor, level=* (or level:ref=*)\r\n    - Node: level=* (or level:ref=*)\r\n- [Elevator](https://wiki.openstreetmap.org/wiki/Tag:highway%3Delevator)\r\n    - Node: tag:highway=elevator, level=* (or level:ref=*)\r\n- [Stairs](https://wiki.openstreetmap.org/wiki/Tag:highway%3Dsteps)\r\n    - Way:  tag:highway=steps, level=* (or level:ref=*), indoor=yes\r\n    - Node: level=* (or level:ref=*), indoor=yes\r\n- [Escalators](https://wiki.openstreetmap.org/wiki/Tag:highway%3Dsteps)\r\n    - Way:  tag:highway=steps, conveying=* , level=* (or level:ref=*), indoor=yes\r\n    - Node: level=* (or level:ref=*), indoor=yes\r\n- [Building Entrance](https://wiki.openstreetmap.org/wiki/Key:entrance) \r\n    - Node: tag:entrance=* ,  level=* (or level:ref=*), indoor=yes\r\n\r\nNotes:\r\n- For vertical elevators, they are mapped as a node in OSM. Wouldn't it be more intuitive to map them as ways (for both vertical and inclined elevators)? I'm curious what folks think.  \r\n- level vs level:ref: level indicates the floor level (i.e. float) while level:ref specifies the ref or name of the level (string). Especially for malls, we would prefer to use the name of the level for maneuver instructions. For example, I would prefer _take the elevator to Ground Floor_ to _take the elevator to Level 0_ .\r\n- We cam reuse TripLeg_Use_kFootwayUse for corridors. We can make new TripLeg_Node_Types for elevators and building entrances, and make new TripLeg_Uses for stairs and escalators. Alternatively, we can reuse TripLeg_Use_kStepsUse for stairs too.\r\n\r\n### Costing for indoor elements\r\nWe need to add PedestrainCost for each indoor element.\r\n\r\n### Maneuver instructions for indoor routes\r\nWe can make new DirectionsLeg_Maneuver_Types for elevators, stairs, escalators and/or building entrances, to provide detailed navigation instructions for pedestrians. \r\n\r\n- Corridors\r\n    - Continue on the walkway.\r\n    - Turn left/right onto the walkway. \r\n- Elevator\r\n    - Take the elevator to Level 1. \r\n- Stairs\r\n    - Take the stairs to Level 1. \r\n- Escalator\r\n    - Take the escalator to Level 1. \r\n- Building Entrance\r\n    - Enter/exit the building and continue on the walkway.\r\n\r\n### References\r\n\r\n- [OSM Simple indoor tagging (SIT)](https://wiki.openstreetmap.org/wiki/Simple_Indoor_Tagging)\r\n- [Apple Indoor Mapping Data Format (IMDF)](https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2019/241/)\r\n- [A Data Model for Using OpenStreetMap to Integrate Indoor and Outdoor Route Planning](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC6068512/)\r\n\r\nDoes this sound like something that valhalla would like to support? I would love to hear if there are any questions/interests/feedbacks around pedestrian indoor routing. I can provide more details/thoughts if folks are interested, and I will be happy to implement it too. \r\n\r\nCC @kevinkreiser, @abhi2039 ","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/3469/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/3469/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla/issues/3691","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valhalla/valhalla","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/va